{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>נדבכין</b> — [He] explained [it as] rows, and the translation is beneath the rows, read pausal for נדבכין. This resembles the first structure, as it says: three courses of hewn stone and a course of cedar beams." "<b>ונפקתא</b> — let it be brought out."], :book :ezra, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {0 "Resolved [He] as the unnamed commentator being cited; the referent is likely a prior exegete such as the Gaon [Saadia]. 'Read pausal for נדבכין' renders מלרע, a reading tradition notation whose exact application here is uncertain."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Ezra -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:42:03.928064956Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}